    {
      "id": "size-shapes-life",
      "real": true,
      "headline": "Why a bigger deer",
      "accent": "breaks.",
      "dek": "If a deer grew five times bigger in every direction, it would weigh 125 times more. Its leg bones would get only 25 times thicker. That is why big animals are built differently from small ones.",
